Subject: DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: log the dcomp subclass DefWindowProc black hole

Not for merge. Instruments the two places where a dcomp-subclassed target
window can end up with no original WndProc to forward to, which sends every
message - including all mouse input - to DefWindowProc. The window keeps
painting, because dcomp blits its content independently of the WndProc, so
the symptom is "paints fine but is completely input-dead" - exactly what the
existing comments in this file describe for JUCE/SWAM editors that recreate
their composition target, and exactly the Splice panel symptom in issue 61.

Splice's panel is a WebView2 composition-hosting target. Collapsing the panel
(double-clicking the divider) makes CHOC build a new host window and move the
webview into it while the WebView2 browser process survives, so a second
CreateTargetForHwnd runs against a window that may already carry our subclass.
If the origproc property is gone at that moment - removed by a WM_NCDESTROY on
a recycled HWND while the subclass survived - orig_wndproc is NULL and the
window becomes the black hole the guard above it was written to prevent.

These two ERRs make that condition observable instead of inferred. Build with
this applied, reproduce, and grep for "BLACK HOLE" / "origproc prop is GONE".
diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/device.c b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
index 059b3de..7cafee0 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -2078,7 +2078,18 @@ static LRESULT CALLBACK dcomp_target_wndproc(HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam,
 
     if (!orig_wndproc && target) orig_wndproc = target->orig_wndproc;
     if (!orig_wndproc)
+    {
+        /* DIAGNOSTIC (issue 61 / Splice panel): our subclass is installed but we
+         * have neither the origproc property nor a target to recover it from, so
+         * every message - including all mouse input - goes to DefWindowProc. The
+         * window keeps painting (dcomp blits its own content) but is input-dead. */
+        static unsigned int blackhole_count;
+        if (!blackhole_count++ || !(blackhole_count % 500))
+            ERR("dcomp subclass BLACK HOLE: hwnd %p msg %#x has no orig_wndproc "
+                "(target %p) - window is input-dead, count %u.\n",
+                hwnd, msg, target, blackhole_count);
         return DefWindowProcW(hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam);
+    }
 
     if (!target)
     {
@@ -2262,6 +2273,10 @@ static HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE dcomp_device_CreateTargetForHwnd(IDCompositionD
         if (cur == dcomp_target_wndproc)
         {
             object->orig_wndproc = (WNDPROC)GetPropW(hwnd, dcomp_origproc_prop);
+            if (!object->orig_wndproc)
+                ERR("dcomp target %p on hwnd %p: subclass already installed but "
+                    "origproc prop is GONE - this window will be input-dead.\n",
+                    object, hwnd);
         }
         else
         {
